# Shader sources are checksum-locked by committed validation reports, which
# hash the bytes on disk. With core.autocrlf=true and no policy here a checkout
# on Windows rewrites them to CRLF while the blob keeps LF, so those hashes
# stop matching — a fresh clone fails the suite before any work starts.
#
# Scoped deliberately to the locked file types. Normalising the whole tree
# would rewrite many files that are not checksum-locked and is a separate
# decision.
*.frag text eol=lf
*.vert text eol=lf
*.glsl text eol=lf
